{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>As he had schemed</b> — and not as he had done. From this the Sages said: \"If they were executed, they are not executed,\" in the language of Rashi (Rashi on Deuteronomy 19:19), from the words of our Rabbis (Makkot 5a). The reason for this is that the judgment of conspiring witnesses is by decree of the Ruler, that they are two against two. Now when two come and testify against Reuben that he killed a person, and two others come and declare them conspiring witnesses against their testimony, Scripture commanded that they [the conspiring witnesses] be executed, for on the merit of Reuben, who was innocent and righteous, this outcome came about. Had he been a wicked man liable to death, HaShem would not have delivered him from the hand of the court, as He said (Exodus 23:7), \"For I will not justify the wicked.\" But if Reuben had already been executed, we reckon that everything the first witnesses testified against him was true, for he died through his own iniquity; had he been righteous, HaShem would not have abandoned him into their hand, as Scripture says (Psalms 37:33), \"HaShem will not abandon him in his hand, and will not condemn him when he is judged.\" Furthermore, HaShem would not grant the righteous judges who stand before Him to shed innocent blood, for judgment belongs to Elohim, and in the midst of Elohim He judges. Now all this is a great distinction for the judges of Israel, and the assurance that the Holy One, blessed is He, acts through them and with them in the matter of judgment. This is the meaning of \"then both parties to the dispute shall stand before HaShem\" (Deuteronomy 19:17) — before HaShem they stand when they come before the priests and the judges, and He guides them in the way of truth. I have already mentioned this in the portion of <i>V'eleh HaMishpatim</i> (Exodus 21:6)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Ramban's gloss 'they are two against two' (שהם שנים ושנים) refers to the requirement that conspiring witnesses be invalidated by another pair of witnesses, per Makkot 5a; rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:52:04.231585011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}